          <h3>Full-stack accountability</h3>
          <p>From fibre to security alerts, one team owns the whole stack. No vendor blaming. No handoff gaps. One escalation path, one phone number.</p>
          <p>When you engage MEAICON, you sign one contract that covers the assessment, the design, the build, and the operations. The team that designs your network architecture is the team that builds it and the team that monitors it at 3am. There is no integrator-to-operator handoff, no vendor-to-vendor blame chain, and no ticket that falls through the gap between "their problem" and "our problem."</p>
          <p>This matters most when things fail. A network outage that traces back to a security policy, a data centre issue that manifests as application latency, a blockchain platform that depends on network segmentation — these cross-layer problems are the hardest to resolve, and they are exactly where fragmented vendor models break down. One team, one accountability, one resolution.</p>
        </article>
