          <h3>Regional delivery, local teams</h3>
          <p>Engineers on the ground in eleven markets spanning the GCC, Africa, South Asia, and North America who understand local regulations, procurement, and operational realities. Not a fly-in team.</p>
          <p>Our delivery teams live and work in the markets they serve. They understand the public-sector procurement cycles, the telecom interconnect frameworks, the data residency requirements, and the operational realities — from climate-hardened enclosures for extreme heat to fibre routes that account for infrastructure maturity. That local depth means fewer surprises, faster mobilisation, and designs that fit the environment they are deployed into.</p>
          <p>Crucially, local delivery does not mean local standards. Every market team follows the same engineering documentation, architecture templates, and quality gates. The difference is local context applied to a shared standard — not a different quality of delivery depending on where you operate.</p>
        </article>
