          <h3>Security as foundation</h3>
          <p>Every capability is built with security as a first principle. Our SOC operates 24/7 alongside our NOC — monitoring threats and performance on the same plane.</p>
          <p>Security is not a layer we add after the network is built or a service we bolt on once the data centre is live. It is designed into the architecture from the first drawing — network segmentation, zero-trust access controls, encrypted transport, and continuous monitoring are specifications, not afterthoughts. The same team that architects your connectivity architects your security posture, so there are no gaps between what the network enables and what the security team can see.</p>
          <p>Our SOC and NOC operate on the same monitoring plane, which means a security anomaly and a performance anomaly are correlated in real time — not investigated in isolation by separate teams with separate tools. When something unusual happens, the network engineer and the security analyst see it together, triage it together, and resolve it together.</p>
        </article>
