          <h3>Engineered for the region</h3>
          <p>our markets have distinct regulatory, climate, and infrastructure realities. Our designs account for heat, dust, sovereignty, and local content from the first drawing.</p>
          <p>The the GCC, Africa, South Asia, and North America present engineering challenges that temperate-region templates do not solve. Data centre cooling loads in 50°C ambient temperatures. Fibre routes through regions with varying infrastructure maturity. Sovereign data residency requirements that prohibit cross-border data flows. Local content regulations that mandate in-country value and local workforce participation. These are not edge cases — they are the baseline.</p>
          <p>Our engineering templates account for these realities from the specification stage, not the change-order stage. We design for the environment you operate in, not a template designed for a different one.</p>
        </article>
